  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened Electoral Systems and Institutions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project seeks to address the challenges outlined to support Member Countries, in particular EMBs, through the implementation of the whole-of-election-cycle approach in accordance with the Revised Commonwealth Guidelines for the Conduct of Election Observation in Member Countries, endorsed by Heads at 2018 CHOGM. This will be achieved through a three-pronged approach which includes election observation, provision of technical assistance and peer-to-peer learning &amp; capacity-building. The project also entails a consistent engagement with Member Countries, including follow-ups on the implementation of previous observer recommendations. The proposed technical assistance builds on the recommendations of previous observer reports. However, some member countries can go successive electoral cycles without implementing observer recommendations on key aspects of the electoral process. The successful implementation of observer recommendations hinge on political will. In view of this, Commonwealth Heads of Government have recommended that countries establish domestic mechanism to take forward the recommendations made by Commonwealth observers. The creation of the election observation recommendations database will allow for better tracking of the level of implementation of recommendations, which in turn will allow for the identification of priority issues and will allow targeted support to countries. EMBs in Commonwealth small states often face capacity and skills gaps, and would have access to a cohort of relevant expertise across the electoral spectrum and would benefit from bespoke technical assistance on request. Pre-election or needs assessment missions/engagements with small states could assist in identifying these gaps.</narrative>
  </description>
